# experiment-repo — analysis

Logistic regression vs k-NN on Iris (OpenML 61), 10 x stratified 5-fold CV.

## Layout
Delivered paths (assignment): `report/code/` and `report/results/`.
- `report/code/` — all code (see its README): `fetch_data.py`, `cv_compare.py`, `run_local.sh`, `ibex_job.sbatch`,
  `compare_runs.py`, `summarize.py`, `requirements.txt`; `data/iris.arff` from
  https://openml.org/data/v1/download/61/iris.arff, md5 `ad484452702105cbf3d30f8deaba39a9` = OpenML `md5_checksum`.
- `report/results/` — `run_local/`, `run_ibex/` (per-fold `folds.csv`, per-case `predictions.csv`, `run.json`, logs),
  `reproducibility.json`, `summary.json`, `table.csv`, `folds_long.csv` (figure input), `numbers.tex` (LaTeX macros).
- `tools/`, `diagnostics/` — working material, not delivered.

## Results (quoted run: local; identical to Ibex)
| | mean acc. | 95% CI (corrected, primary) | 95% CI (naive) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Multinomial LR | 0.9540 | [0.9156, 0.9924] | [0.9435, 0.9645] |
| k-NN (inner-CV k) | 0.9447 | [0.8946, 0.9947] | [0.9311, 0.9583] |
| LR − k-NN (paired) | +0.0093 | [−0.0251, +0.0438] | [−0.0001, +0.0187] |

- No detectable difference: the corrected interval of the paired difference covers 0 (corrected t p = 0.59);
  LR better on 16 folds, tie on 25, k-NN better on 9. The naive interval nearly excludes 0 only because it ignores
  the dependence between folds.
- Selected k spans 1–21 (median 8, mode 9) over 50 folds: inner-CV accuracy is flat in k on Iris.
- Robustness, no standardization: LR 0.9633, k-NN 0.9560, difference +0.0073 [−0.0192, +0.0339]; same conclusion.
- LR: 0 convergence warnings.

## Reproducibility
Ibex SLURM job 53912439, partition `batch`, node **cn113-35-l** (AMD EPYC 7702), Python 3.11.0; local: sandbox
container, Python 3.11.2; identical numpy 2.1.3 / scipy 1.14.1 / scikit-learn 1.5.2 / pandas 2.2.3.
`folds.csv` and `predictions.csv` are byte-identical between the runs (md5 `d5f5a844…`, `83320bcb…`); 0 of 50 folds
and 0 of 6000 predictions differ (`report/results/reproducibility.json`).

## Deviations from plan.md §2
- k grid 1..30 (all integers) instead of the suggested odd 1..29; ties broken to the smallest k.
- The data file is fetched by `fetch_data.py` before the runs (the job containers have no network); both runs assert
  the OpenML md5.
